# Normalize line endings. Added in Step 117, before the first commit
# made from a Windows working tree.
#
# Why: app.js was re-saved by a Windows editor and switched from LF to
# CRLF. Its content did not change by a single character, but every one
# of its 180 lines then showed as modified — 9870 bytes committed vs
# 10050 bytes on disk, the difference being exactly one \r per line.
# Committing that would have written a 180-line diff into the history of
# this project's most safety-critical wiring file for no semantic
# change, and would have repeated for every file any Windows editor
# touched.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` tells git to store every text file with LF in the
# repository regardless of what the working tree uses, so the working
# copy can keep CRLF locally and still produce clean diffs. The repo has
# no binary files today; the explicit entries below simply make the
# intent unambiguous for the file types that exist.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.js   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.example text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
.nvmrc text eol=lf
